  {
    "_note": "Ring Road (T50), after briefs/ring-road.md with every question at its recommendation: speedboats round a small Saturn on its rings, one lap of about 2.5 km from Ring Station on the B ring. The lane jumps out across the Cassini Division near 41 degrees and back near 312, a floating ramp before each gap; buoys light power arrows on the A ring only, so the shorter way round on the B ring gets none; gold rings over the crest of the bending wave; canisters round the lap. Off the ice is a wipeout.",
    "name": "race.ring_road",
    "place": "place.saturn",
    "weather": "weather.ring_day",
